00:32:00.920 --> 00:32:05.600
are able to make a difference
to a country in need

00:32:05.600 --> 00:32:09.860
of open education resources.

00:32:09.860 --> 00:32:11.450
Greetings, greetings, everyone.

00:32:11.450 --> 00:32:15.760
I cannot even begin to tell you
how happy I am to be here this

00:32:15.760 --> 00:32:19.300
morning, or afternoon,
representing Edward Waters

00:32:19.300 --> 00:32:23.050
University on this wonderful
open education journey.

00:32:23.050 --> 00:32:26.590
I want to thank our two
affiliate institutions,

00:32:26.590 --> 00:32:30.610
Lawson State Community, college
and Denmark Technical College

00:32:30.610 --> 00:32:33.670
for joining with
us in this effort .

00:32:33.670 --> 00:32:37.300
Our main priority is to
make a college education

00:32:37.300 --> 00:32:42.460
attainable and accessible to
as many students as possible

00:32:42.460 --> 00:32:46.000
through OER, because we
believe that education

00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:48.310
is a fundamental human right.

00:32:48.310 --> 00:32:51.550
Therefore, we should
not allow anything

00:32:51.550 --> 00:32:55.900
to hinder the success of anyone
or any group in their pursuit

00:32:55.900 --> 00:32:56.840
of an education.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:32:58.850
And that's why we're here today.

00:32:58.850 --> 00:33:03.820
Edward Waters University is
distinctively Florida's oldest

00:33:03.820 --> 00:33:06.310
independent institution of
higher education, higher

00:33:06.310 --> 00:33:10.090
learning, as well as the
state's first institution

00:33:10.090 --> 00:33:14.110
established for the education
of African-Americans.

00:33:14.110 --> 00:33:19.150
From the beginning, EWU was
faced with both abject poverty

00:33:19.150 --> 00:33:23.560
and widespread illiteracy
among its constituents, which

00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:27.160
explains why, even today,
90% of our students

00:33:27.160 --> 00:33:29.050
are Pell Grant recipients.

00:33:29.050 --> 00:33:34.370
Thus, what Dr. Robbie
Melton and Dr. Gerry Hanley

00:33:34.370 --> 00:33:38.600
are doing for the HBCU community
as they facilitate access

00:33:38.600 --> 00:33:42.380
for our students to open
educational resources

00:33:42.380 --> 00:33:45.290
is beyond miraculous.

00:33:45.290 --> 00:33:50.060
This is why I'm so excited
to report that our first OER

00:33:50.060 --> 00:33:53.750
workshop at EWU, which
was held over a week ago,

00:33:53.750 --> 00:33:57.350
was attended by about
90% of the faculty.

00:33:57.350 --> 00:33:59.150
Pretty remarkable.

00:33:59.150 --> 00:34:02.900
And so our local ARS
team is now motivated

00:34:02.900 --> 00:34:06.980
to gather data to add to the
MERLOT's cultural collection,

00:34:06.980 --> 00:34:09.949
because we do have
a story to tell.

00:34:09.949 --> 00:34:13.400
We are also looking to
extend this opportunity

00:34:13.400 --> 00:34:17.630
to developing countries such as
Haiti, where higher education

00:34:17.630 --> 00:34:19.670
is literally a luxury.

00:34:19.670 --> 00:34:22.909
I should know, because
I'm originally from there.

00:34:22.909 --> 00:34:25.980
I remember when I
was in high school,

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:36.000
I had to copy textbook chapters
by hand to prepare for an exam,

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:39.010
and that was on a regular basis.

00:34:39.010 --> 00:34:46.020
So I don't have to tell you
that this opportunity would

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:50.070
be like manna from heaven
for the Haitian students.

00:34:50.070 --> 00:34:51.210
Thank you, Abby.

00:34:51.210 --> 00:34:54.360
Thank you, Gerry.

00:34:54.360 --> 00:34:56.280
So what we're
doing in our campus

00:34:56.280 --> 00:34:58.770
is making sure that
everybody understands.

00:34:58.770 --> 00:35:00.360
My responsibility,
personally, is

00:35:00.360 --> 00:35:06.280
to convey this key message to
show our students that we care.

00:35:06.280 --> 00:35:07.680
We care for their success.

00:35:07.680 --> 00:35:09.610
We care for their education.

00:35:09.610 --> 00:35:14.850
And that's why I am so excited
about the level of involvement

00:35:14.850 --> 00:35:18.630
of my faculty and the
leadership at the university.

00:35:18.630 --> 00:35:20.100
So we are ready.

00:35:20.100 --> 00:35:21.630
We are equipped.

00:35:21.630 --> 00:35:24.640
And we are thankful for
being on this journey.

00:35:24.640 --> 00:35:28.310
Thank you, everybody.

00:35:28.310 --> 00:35:29.750
And we thank you.

00:35:29.750 --> 00:35:33.920
And again, you see the purpose
for cultural collection.

00:35:33.920 --> 00:35:37.160
You see the purpose of
open education resources.

00:35:37.160 --> 00:35:42.740
And yet, every day we upload,
we search, just like you all

00:35:42.740 --> 00:35:45.590
are doing now for the
Ukraine, so that we

00:35:45.590 --> 00:35:48.960
can have a cultural collection
built. At this time,

00:35:48.960 --> 00:35:53.240
it is my pleasure to
bring on [INAUDIBLE],,

00:35:53.240 --> 00:35:57.290
and you will see for
their graduate program

00:35:57.290 --> 00:36:00.350
the impact of open
education resources.

00:36:13.040 --> 00:36:14.600
Good afternoon.

00:36:14.600 --> 00:36:18.680
Maintaining the spirit of
our founder, Dr. Mary MacLeod

00:36:18.680 --> 00:36:21.350
Bethune, Bethune-Cookman
University

00:36:21.350 --> 00:36:26.240
allows collaboration to bolster
the infusion of open education

00:36:26.240 --> 00:36:29.780
resources in undergraduate
and graduate courses,

00:36:29.780 --> 00:36:33.110
not only on our campus in
Daytona Beach, Florida,

00:36:33.110 --> 00:36:38.570
but with external partners,
Simmons College of Kentucky,

00:36:38.570 --> 00:36:41.610
and Florida A&amp;M University.

00:36:41.610 --> 00:36:44.610
Currently, 12 graduate
faculty members

00:36:44.610 --> 00:36:49.170
are revamping courses to feature
open education resources,

00:36:49.170 --> 00:36:53.430
or function as an
OER only course.

00:36:55.950 --> 00:36:57.025
Next slide, please.

00:37:02.830 --> 00:37:06.870
A few strategies undertaken
by us to propel forward

00:37:06.870 --> 00:37:11.700
include converting all
general education courses

00:37:11.700 --> 00:37:17.350
to open education
resources, persuading

00:37:17.350 --> 00:37:21.850
six of eight graduate programs
and all graduate programs

00:37:21.850 --> 00:37:24.820
offering online degrees
and certificates

00:37:24.820 --> 00:37:31.790
to include OER, or fully
convert courses to OER.

00:37:31.790 --> 00:37:35.360
Currently, there are more
than 50 faculty members

00:37:35.360 --> 00:37:39.410
who have MERLOT accounts.

00:37:39.410 --> 00:37:43.490
We continue to recruit
faculty across our partner

00:37:43.490 --> 00:37:45.810
universities.

00:37:45.810 --> 00:37:47.910
Sharing recordings
that highlight

00:37:47.910 --> 00:37:51.480
discipline specific
OER with faculty

00:37:51.480 --> 00:37:54.130
is another proven strategy.

00:37:54.130 --> 00:37:58.950
And finally, being recognized
for our OER efforts

00:37:58.950 --> 00:38:03.420
have all assisted in
moving us forward.

00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:05.380
Thank you.

00:38:05.380 --> 00:38:08.200
Ladies and gentlemen,
did you hear that?

00:38:08.200 --> 00:38:14.440
The general Ed Corps, all open
education, graduate programs.

00:38:14.440 --> 00:38:19.040
Now you can see together
how we can share.

00:38:19.040 --> 00:38:23.920
So with that, I bring
you Morehouse College.

00:38:23.920 --> 00:38:26.920
Take it away, Dr. Earl-Lewis.

00:38:26.920 --> 00:38:29.740
Good afternoon, and
greetings, colleagues.

00:38:29.740 --> 00:38:32.920
I bring you greetings on
behalf of Dr. David A. Thomas,

00:38:32.920 --> 00:38:36.340
the 12th president of
Morehouse College Dr. Kendrick

00:38:36.340 --> 00:38:40.720
Brown, Provost and Senior Vice
President for Academic Affairs,

00:38:40.720 --> 00:38:44.260
and Dr. Clarissa
Myrick-Harris, the Chair

00:38:44.260 --> 00:38:46.720
of the Division of Humanities.

00:38:46.720 --> 00:38:51.760
This is how our OER program is
anchored at Morehouse College,

00:38:51.760 --> 00:38:55.660
and moving forward with our
partners, Claflin University,

00:38:55.660 --> 00:39:00.370
Clark Atlanta University, and
our newest partner, Livingstone

00:39:00.370 --> 00:39:01.660
College.

00:39:01.660 --> 00:39:04.030
I, like Dr.
McEacran, began using

00:39:04.030 --> 00:39:07.480
open educational resources
as a response to having

00:39:07.480 --> 00:39:10.330
culturally relevant
pedagogical content

00:39:10.330 --> 00:39:12.250
as a part of my own
learning, and then,

00:39:12.250 --> 00:39:15.130
again, when I became a
member of the faculty

00:39:15.130 --> 00:39:17.560
at Florida Memorial University.

00:39:17.560 --> 00:39:23.590
Today at Morehouse College, next
slide, please, our key mission,

00:39:23.590 --> 00:39:26.920
our key message
is mission driven.

00:39:26.920 --> 00:39:29.500
The mission of Morehouse
College is the development

00:39:29.500 --> 00:39:32.830
with disciplined minds, who
will lead lives of leadership

00:39:32.830 --> 00:39:36.580
and service, with special
responsibility for advancing

00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:39.920
knowledge of Black life
history and culture.

00:39:39.920 --> 00:39:44.290
So how are we doing OER
at Morehouse College?

00:39:44.290 --> 00:39:47.950
We are engaging it in
teaching and learning, faculty

00:39:47.950 --> 00:39:50.650
development, and
service learning.

00:39:50.650 --> 00:39:52.900
Let me share a few examples.

00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:57.580
As a part of the teaching and
learning, 100% of the Africana

00:39:57.580 --> 00:40:01.870
Studies faculty and affiliated
faculty within the departments

00:40:01.870 --> 00:40:05.530
of English, history,
journalism, religion

00:40:05.530 --> 00:40:09.770
and philosophy, cinema,
television, and emerging media,

00:40:09.770 --> 00:40:14.680
music, mathematics, computer
science, business and economics

00:40:14.680 --> 00:40:19.100
are using affordable
learning solutions.

00:40:19.100 --> 00:40:23.240
As a part of our
fall 2021 semester,

00:40:23.240 --> 00:40:29.810
we offered 35 sections of our
FYE general education courses.

00:40:29.810 --> 00:40:34.490
15 sections of those courses,
the African-American experience

00:40:34.490 --> 00:40:37.730
and introduction to
Africana Studies,

00:40:37.730 --> 00:40:43.340
representing approximately
45% of the FYE courses

00:40:43.340 --> 00:40:46.300
were all OER.

00:40:46.300 --> 00:40:48.970
With this in mind, we
estimate that we had

00:40:48.970 --> 00:40:53.680
a savings of $2,250 per course.

00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:58.300
This resulted in
approximately $33,750

00:40:58.300 --> 00:41:01.390
worth of savings for students
during the fall semester

00:41:01.390 --> 00:41:04.420
who were enrolled in
our general education

00:41:04.420 --> 00:41:07.840
courses, the
African-American Experience.

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:10.570
But students, what
is the impact?

00:41:10.570 --> 00:41:13.840
What I am learning,
both anecdotally

00:41:13.840 --> 00:41:17.260
and through the data, is that
students remain surprised

00:41:17.260 --> 00:41:21.640
that their learning can begin
before the first day of class,

00:41:21.640 --> 00:41:25.630
by having access to open
educational resources and tools

00:41:25.630 --> 00:41:27.640
to support their learning.

00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:31.960
Within our partnerships, as
we are moving with the faculty

00:41:31.960 --> 00:41:34.900
development piece, we
have engaged a partner

00:41:34.900 --> 00:41:38.110
through A Healing Paradigm,
which is a local wellness

00:41:38.110 --> 00:41:40.150
and psychological
services center,

00:41:40.150 --> 00:41:43.540
and Dr. Kevin Coakley
at UT Austin, who

00:41:43.540 --> 00:41:48.430
created an open source
culturally relevant text

00:41:48.430 --> 00:41:52.720
called Making Black Lives
Matter, Confronting Anti-Bias

00:41:52.720 --> 00:41:53.930
and Racism.

00:41:53.930 --> 00:41:57.460
We're using that text as
a foundational resource

00:41:57.460 --> 00:42:02.290
for facilitating understanding,
as well as providing knowledge.

00:42:02.290 --> 00:42:04.870
It is well researched,
open source,

00:42:04.870 --> 00:42:07.870
and includes the voices of
both undergraduate and graduate

00:42:07.870 --> 00:42:09.220
students.

00:42:09.220 --> 00:42:12.470
As a part of OER commitment
to service learning,

00:42:12.470 --> 00:42:14.710
our [INAUDIBLE] Office
for Community Service

00:42:14.710 --> 00:42:19.660
engages OER through the use
of our Apple Initiative.

00:42:19.660 --> 00:42:22.900
They engage coding
and creativity

00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:25.540
and all of the Apple
learning resources

00:42:25.540 --> 00:42:28.960
as a part of their service
learning, in a one-credit lab,

00:42:28.960 --> 00:42:31.570
as well as a three-hour course.

00:42:31.570 --> 00:42:35.110
They all become Apple teachers,
improve their technology

00:42:35.110 --> 00:42:37.960
skills, learn how
to prototype apps,

00:42:37.960 --> 00:42:42.760
and do this service
in our communities.

00:42:42.760 --> 00:42:46.860
We are excited to continue this
partnership as we move forward,

00:42:46.860 --> 00:42:49.230
and our Office of
Academic Affairs

00:42:49.230 --> 00:42:53.490
is providing fiscal resources
to support faculty research,

00:42:53.490 --> 00:42:57.540
course redesign, and
student internships

00:42:57.540 --> 00:43:02.040
to conduct research
utilizing ALS.

00:43:02.040 --> 00:43:05.550
So please join us in
visiting the HBCU culture

00:43:05.550 --> 00:43:07.920
collection to learn
more about Morehouse

00:43:07.920 --> 00:43:10.710
and our esteemed alumni.

00:43:10.710 --> 00:43:14.110
Thank you so much
for being here today.

00:43:14.110 --> 00:43:15.640
And we thank you so much.

00:43:15.640 --> 00:43:18.850
And again, everyone, everyone,
we only got a few more minutes,

00:43:18.850 --> 00:43:19.750
OK?

00:43:19.750 --> 00:43:24.700
Remember, all that we have
shared is available for you

00:43:24.700 --> 00:43:26.950
right now.

00:43:26.950 --> 00:43:31.000
So again, they're
going to enter the URL

00:43:31.000 --> 00:43:35.320
for the HBCU affordable
learning solution,

00:43:35.320 --> 00:43:40.780
